      "rationale": "Worst 20d momentum in the book (-6.1%) with a moderate interval (0.0534); held slightly below the 7.0% baseline. Financials exposure retained via A15 at minimal size.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A09",
      "target_weight": 0.11,
      "rationale": "Bond ETF with the second-tightest interval (0.0428) acting as ballast alongside cash during the drawdown alert; held at 11% vs 8.7% baseline despite -4.8% 20d, since low width means low uncertainty, not a directional signal.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A05",
      "target_weight": 0.02,
      "rationale": "Gold has the widest ETF interval (0.0891), 25% annualized volatility and -6.3% 20d — it is not behaving as a hedge recently; kept near zero vs 4.2% baseline.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A01",
      "target_weight": 0.03,
      "rationale": "Widest interval of all 15 assets (0.1063) and highest volatility (27.7% ann.); single-stock cap is 10% but forecast uncertainty argues for a small weight near the 3.5% baseline despite +3.0% 20d.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
